  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Prashanth R.R.Enterprises, vs The State Of Telangana on 13 June, 2025 Author: N.Tukaramji Bench: N.Tukaramji The Honourable Sri Justice N.Tukaramji Criminal Petition No. 7019Of 2025 Order",
    "facts": "This Criminal Petition is filed under Section 528 of BharatiyaNagarikSurakshaSanhita, 2023 (for short 'BNSS, 2023') seeking quashment of the proceedings , against the petitioner in Crime No.81of 2025 of SangemPolice Station, Warangal District. 2. The petitioner is sole accusedin Crime No.81 of 2025registered for the offences punishable under Sections 272&275 read with 3(5)of BharatiyaNyayaSanhita, 2023 (for short 'BNS, 2023'). 3. 4. The prosecution case in brief is that the petitioner/accused is involved in selling and purchasing the banned Tobacco products and the Police concerned seized the said Tobacco products, total worth of Rs.1,48,070/-. 8. As per the prosecution,on 13.05.2025 at 07.00 hours, the complainant/Sub Inspector lodged a complaint alleging that the petitioner is running a kirana shop at Gavicherla Village, SangemMandal, and by purchasing tobacco products banned by the Government from unknown persons andselling the same at his kirana shop. Accordingly, the complainant and his staff apprehended the petitioner and seized tobacco products viz., 1)Anaru Packets-15 x 500= Rs.7,500/-, Prashanth R.R.Enterprises, vs The State Of Telangana on 13 June, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/173504774/ Thereafter, the Director General of Police, Telangana State issued Circular Memorandum in RC.No.295/R1-NS/2022 with directions to the Station House Officers not to interfere with the business activities, who carry out the business as per rules of Food Safety and Standards Authority of India and also not to take any coercive measures against the tobacco traders as long as the order of the Hon'ble Supreme Court is in force.",
    "arguments": "5. Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the Coordinate Bench of this Court vide Criminal Petition Nos.3731 and Batch [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioners therein by 2 NTR,J passing common order dated 27.08.2018. He further submits that the 2nd respondent has registered the present crime in violation of the orders passed by this Court. Hence, prayed for quashment of the proceedings against the petitioner in the crime. 6. Learned Additional Public Prosecutor would submit thatthe petitioner has to face either investigation or trial and prove his innocence and instead of doing so, he has filed the present criminal petition, which cannot be considered at this stage. 7.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "5. Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the Coordinate Bench of this Court vide Criminal Petition Nos.3731 and Batch [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioners therein by 2 NTR,J passing common order dated 27.08.2018. He further submits that the 2nd respondent has registered the present crime in violation of the orders passed by this Court. Hence, prayed for quashment of the proceedings against the petitioner in the crime. 6. Learned Additional Public Prosecutor would submit thatthe petitioner has to face either investigation or trial and prove his innocence and instead of doing so, he has filed the present criminal petition, which cannot be considered at this stage. 7.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
